{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# RCA — store wedge that stranded local ticket events off origin (P0, RESOLVED — no permanent loss)\n\n## Symptom\nrebar ticket writes (incl. the akitainu completion attestation) were not reaching\n`origin/tickets`. The shared local store sat **28 commits ahead / 125 behind** origin and\nfalling further behind; the akitainu close kept failing the completion-verifier gate because\nits attestation never landed on origin.\n\n## Proven root cause (two artifacts, one systemic defect)\n**(1) Upstream — compaction leaves the tracker working tree dirty, non-atomically.**\n`_compact_locked()` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:449-466`) writes `SNAPSHOT.json`,\nrenames sources to `*.retired`, and only *afterward* `git add -A` + commits; the lock releases\nin `finally`. There is **no rollback** around the write/rename. Since `d2dea317ec` this runs in\na **detached background sweep** (`compact_trigger.py:287-318 _spawn_detached_sweep`) spawned from\nthe close. If that worker is SIGKILLed / times out / the parent exits after mutate-before-commit,\nthe working tree is left dirty: untracked `SNAPSHOT.json` + `*.retired` + `.tmp-event-*`, and\nworking-tree-deleted `.archived` files. Nothing runs `git checkout`/`git clean` on worker death.\n\n**(2) Wedge — reconverge's union-merge cannot tolerate those untracked leftovers.**\n`_union_merge` (`src/rebar/_store/sync.py:182-190`) runs `git merge origin/tickets`. Another\nclone already compacted the *same* tickets and pushed those `.retired`/`SNAPSHOT` paths to\norigin, so the merge must **create** those paths — but they already exist **untracked** in the\nworking tree → git aborts *\"untracked working tree files would be overwritten by merge.\"*\nFailure handling is abort-only (`sync.py:191-197`); push-recovery `_recover_dirty_merge`\n(`push_recovery.py:136-143`) uses `git reset --hard` (tracked-only, explicit *\"untracked files\nare left alone\"*) and `_stash_create` (`push_recovery.py:55-68`, **no `-u`**), so it cannot clear\nuntracked files. Every retry re-aborts identically → permanent wedge → local commits never reach\norigin, lost if the worktree is removed.\n\n## Discriminating evidence / proof\n- Reset/reconverge path exonerated: scanned all 33,621 reflog entries / 2,194 resets in the\n  shared tracker — **0 unsafe resets** (every one a safe FF-adopt). Not the loss vector.\n- Isolated runtime repro (`/tmp/mergerepro`): reproduced the exact `git merge` abort (exit 2);\n  confirmed `git stash` **without** `-u` reports \"No local changes to save\" and does NOT rescue\n  it; confirmed both `git stash -u` and `git clean` of the regenerable leftovers unblock the\n  merge while preserving the unique local commit.\n- Topology: ~90 `.tickets-tracker` dirs are separate worktrees sharing **one** `.git`\n  (inode 976794618) → one HEAD (f36a24a9de) → one object store. One shared wedge surfaced at\n  ~90 paths.\n\n## defect_legitimacy = `defect`\nViolates the non-destructive reconverge invariant stated in `sync.py`'s own header and the\nAGENTS.md contract \"the store shares every write immediately (auto-commit + auto-push)\".\n\n## Recovery performed (TOP priority — DONE, verified)\nUnder rebar's exclusive `write_lock(tracker)`: backed up + preserved all 232 untracked files\n(incl. 6 `.tmp-event-*`), `git checkout -- .` (restored 115 deleted `.archived`), removed the\nregenerable untracked leftovers, `git merge origin/tickets` (union), verified **all 28** stranded\nevent files present (incl. akitainu attestation `55cb8610`), pushed to origin.\n**Result: ahead=0 / behind=0; attestation + all 28 events on origin; tree clean; live write\nround-trip confirmed.**\n\n## No permanent data loss\nThe 6 orphaned `.tmp-event-*` were triaged: 2 were prior-session debug probes; the other 4\n(a REVIEW_RESULT PASS, a regression COMMENT, two description EDITs) each have their content\nalready committed on origin under a **retry uuid** (superseding review PASS on `06e0`; comment +\nedit on `0d15`; edit on `e30d`). Every stranded write reached origin via retry. Backup retained\nat the recorded /tmp path until fully closed out.\n\n## Out of scope (separate products, not this store)\n`parity-scan/.tickets-tracker` → `github.com/navapbc/flex-parity-scan`;\n`digital-service-orchestra/.tickets-tracker` → its own repo. Both are different products' stores\n(may share the bug class); not touched. d-s-o had ahead=0 (no loss).\n\n## Fix plan (secondary priority — see description)\nPrimary: make reconverge/push-recovery robust to stale untracked leftovers (relocate/clean\ncolliding untracked paths before the union merge). Defense-in-depth: make compaction crash-atomic\n(roll back the dirty tree on worker death). RED→GREEN, held-out oracle + mutation check; land via\nGerrit."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786674133885567001,"uuid":"91e329ec-924e-467f-af97-da7d51224d29"}